["I need to make 24 using 10, 1, 2, 6 with each number once.\n\nLet me try different combinations.\n\n10 + 1 + 2 + 6 = 19, no.\n10 * 1 * 2 + 6 = 26, no.\n10 + 1 * 2 * 6 = 22, no.\n10 * 2 + 6 - 1 = 25, no.\n10 * 2 - 6 + 1 = 15, no.\n10 * 2 - 6 * 1 = 14, no.\n10 * 2 + 6 * 1 = 26, no.\n10 * 2 + 6 - 1 = 25, no.\n10 * 2 - 6 + 1 = 15, no.\n(10 - 6) * (1 + 2) = 4 * 3 = 12, no.\n(10 - 6) * 2 * 1 = 8, no.\n(10 - 6) * 2 + 1 = 9, no.\n(10 + 2) * (6 - 1) = 12 * 5 = 60, no.\n(10 + 2) * 6 * 1 = 72, no.\n(10 + 2) * 6 / 1 = 72, no.\n(10 - 2) * (6 - 1) = 8 * 5 = 40, no.\n(10 - 2) * 6 * 1 = 48, no.\n(10 - 2) * 6 / 1 = 48, no.\n(10 - 2) * 6 - 1 = 47, no.\n(10 - 2) * 6 + 1 = 49, no.\n(10 + 1) * 2 + 6 = 28, no.\n(10 + 1) * 2 - 6 = 16, no.\n(10 + 1) * 2 * 6 = 132, no.\n(10 - 1) * 2 + 6 = 24! Yes!\n\nLet me verify: (10 - 1) * 2 + 6 = 9 * 2 + 6 = 18 + 6 = 24. Yes!\n\nSo the answer is (10 - 1) * 2 + 6.\n"]